1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:03,451
Few places on Earth are
as closed off as this one.

2
00:00:04,261 --> 00:00:07,211
This is North Korea, known
as the Hermit Kingdom.

3
00:00:07,661 --> 00:00:09,181
Its capital is Pyongyang.

4
00:00:10,831 --> 00:00:15,455
About 26 million people live here,
on 120,000 square kilometers.

5
00:00:17,105 --> 00:00:18,364
They speak Korean.

6
00:00:18,414 --> 00:00:19,674
Hello is annyeong.

7
00:00:21,324 --> 00:00:23,154
And they pay with the North Korean won.

8
00:00:25,633 --> 00:00:26,616
Some fun facts.

9
00:00:26,666 --> 00:00:30,543
And stay until the end,
for a mystery nobody ever solved.

10
00:00:32,050 --> 00:00:35,051
North Korea once had its own calendar.

11
00:00:35,101 --> 00:00:40,511
From 1997 to 2024, years were counted
from the birth of Kim Il Sung.

12
00:00:41,061 --> 00:00:44,975
In 2015, North Korea moved
its clocks back 30 minutes,

13
00:00:45,025 --> 00:00:47,104
and called it Pyongyang Time.

14
00:00:47,154 --> 00:00:49,013
In 2018, it switched back.

15
00:00:49,563 --> 00:00:52,747
The Pyongyang metro
is about 100 meters underground.

16
00:00:52,797 --> 00:00:55,234
The escalator ride takes over 3 minutes.

17
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:58,330
Now, a few surprising places.

18
00:00:59,883 --> 00:01:05,068
In Pyongyang stands the Ryugyong
Hotel, a pyramid 330 meters tall.

19
00:01:05,118 --> 00:01:08,400
Building started in 1987, stopped in 1992,

20
00:01:08,450 --> 00:01:11,731
and the outside was only finished in 2011.

21
00:01:12,281 --> 00:01:17,466
On the Chinese border, Mount Paektu hides
Heaven Lake inside a volcanic crater.

22
00:01:17,516 --> 00:01:20,117
The volcano erupted around the year 946.

23
00:01:20,667 --> 00:01:22,822
Mount Kumgang, the Diamond Mountain,

24
00:01:22,872 --> 00:01:25,639
joined the UNESCO World
Heritage list in 2025.

25
00:01:26,189 --> 00:01:28,971
Kaesong was the capital
of the Goryeo dynasty.

26
00:01:29,021 --> 00:01:32,295
Its historic monuments joined
the UNESCO list in 2013.

27
00:01:36,433 --> 00:01:38,246
So, what does $10 get you here?

28
00:01:39,783 --> 00:01:44,224
First, visitors pay in dollars,
euros or yuan, not in won.

29
00:01:44,274 --> 00:01:48,327
A draft beer in a Pyongyang
bar costs about 50 cents.

30
00:01:48,877 --> 00:01:51,219
A metro ride costs just a few cents.

31
00:01:51,769 --> 00:01:55,182
A pint at a hotel
microbrewery is about $2.

32
00:01:55,732 --> 00:01:58,101
A short taxi ride is about $5.

33
00:01:58,651 --> 00:02:03,371
But 10 minutes of Wi-Fi costs
about $1.70, more than 3 beers.

34
00:02:03,921 --> 00:02:08,545
So with $10, you get a beer,
a metro ride, a craft pint, a taxi,

35
00:02:08,595 --> 00:02:11,101
10 minutes online, and some change.

36
00:02:12,067 --> 00:02:13,586
Now, the don't list.

37
00:02:15,150 --> 00:02:17,153
Don't wander off on your own.

38
00:02:17,203 --> 00:02:20,693
Visitors must stay
with their guides at all times.

39
00:02:21,243 --> 00:02:23,019
Don't take photos without asking.

40
00:02:23,069 --> 00:02:26,338
Soldiers, checkpoints
and construction sites are off limits.

41
00:02:26,888 --> 00:02:30,381
Don't pack a drone,
or a guidebook about North Korea.

42
00:02:30,431 --> 00:02:31,851
Customs can take both.

43
00:02:32,401 --> 00:02:34,236
Don't joke about the leaders.

44
00:02:34,286 --> 00:02:36,381
Insults are taken very seriously.

45
00:02:36,931 --> 00:02:40,488
And don't fold or throw away a newspaper
with a leader's picture on it.

46
00:02:40,538 --> 00:02:43,791
Visitors can be arrested
for not treating those images with care.

47
00:02:44,733 --> 00:02:45,895
Let's talk about culture.

48
00:02:47,450 --> 00:02:52,268
A famous dish is Pyongyang naengmyeon:
cold buckwheat noodles in a cold broth,

49
00:02:52,318 --> 00:02:54,453
served at the Okryugwan restaurant.

50
00:02:55,003 --> 00:02:57,720
The traditional outfit
is the chima jeogori,

51
00:02:57,770 --> 00:03:00,110
a short jacket with a long wide skirt.

52
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:03,059
A traditional instrument is the gayageum,

53
00:03:03,109 --> 00:03:05,747
a long zither played
by plucking its strings.

54
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:07,704
Time for a little history.

55
00:03:09,217 --> 00:03:13,561
In 1948, 3 years after Korea was split
in two, North Korea was founded,

56
00:03:13,611 --> 00:03:15,417
with Pyongyang as its capital.

57
00:03:15,968 --> 00:03:19,083
In 1953, an armistice
stopped the Korean War.

58
00:03:19,133 --> 00:03:21,334
A peace treaty was never signed.

59
00:03:21,884 --> 00:03:25,613
In 2006, North Korea carried
out its first nuclear test.

60
00:03:26,567 --> 00:03:30,882
And now, the chapter you were all
waiting for: legends and mysteries.

61
00:03:32,450 --> 00:03:37,018
Legend says a god's son, Hwanung,
came down to Mount Paektu.

62
00:03:37,068 --> 00:03:40,789
A bear and a tiger begged
him to make them human.

63
00:03:40,839 --> 00:03:46,639
He told them to stay in a cave for 100
days, eating only garlic and mugwort.

64
00:03:46,689 --> 00:03:50,256
The tiger gave up,
but the bear became a woman.

65
00:03:50,306 --> 00:03:55,028
Her son, Dangun, founded the first
Korean kingdom, in 2333 BC.

66
00:03:55,578 --> 00:03:57,836
Another legend tells of Chollima,

67
00:03:57,886 --> 00:04:01,403
a winged horse so fast
that no rider could tame it.

68
00:04:01,453 --> 00:04:06,020
It was said to run 1,000 ri
in a single day, about 400 kilometers.

69
00:04:06,070 --> 00:04:11,825
In the 1950s, North Korea made it a symbol
of rebuilding the country at full speed.

70
00:04:11,875 --> 00:04:17,071
Today, a bronze Chollima stands 46
meters high, on Mansu Hill in Pyongyang.

71
00:04:17,621 --> 00:04:19,057
And now, the mystery.

72
00:04:19,107 --> 00:04:24,081
Heaven Lake fills the crater of Mount
Paektu, on the border with China.

73
00:04:24,131 --> 00:04:28,114
In 1903, people said a huge
creature rose from the water.

74
00:04:28,164 --> 00:04:31,298
In 1962, more than 100
people reported seeing

75
00:04:31,348 --> 00:04:34,553
two shapes chasing each
other across the lake.

76
00:04:34,603 --> 00:04:37,595
Skeptics say it was floating
volcanic rock,

77
00:04:37,645 --> 00:04:40,355
but nobody has ever proved what it was.

78
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,435
That was North Korea.

79
00:04:45,485 --> 00:04:47,577
Which country should we visit next?

80
00:04:47,627 --> 00:04:49,046
Tell me in the comments.

